      <processInformation>
        <referenceFunction amount="1" category="electronics" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="This dataset can be applied to describe the production of a typical network cable for computers. The total weight of 1 m of network cable is 0.036 kg (without the belonging plugs). The information for this dataset is based on weighing, measurements and analysis at EMPA Laboratories. In 2023, only production efforts data are updated. Furthermore, material and energy input are now represented by global inventory flows; UUID: d9fad792-5b9f-39d5-814e-d15fd9a767ac" includedProcesses="Describes the production of a typical network cable used with desktop or laptop computers. Calculated per 1 m of connector. Included are the materials copper, soft PVC, LDPE and tin (as coating) with their respective manufacturing processes. The infrastructure is calculated via the proxy &quot;electronic component production plant&quot;. Further inventoried are the electricity for the assembly of the connector, the fuel oil, propane and water input, the disposal of plastic and rubber parts, the VOC and methanol emissions created during the processing, plus the road and rail transportation for input materials from the regional storage to the production site. The accumulated hazardous waste is also reported." infrastructureIncluded="false" infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="electronics" localName="Cable, network cable, category 5, without plugs, at plant" localSubCategory="devices" name="Cable, network cable, category 5, without plugs, at plant" subCategory="devices" unit="m">
